1.3 Permutation values
======================

Functions return permutations as ‘pgrp_perm’ values, shown in cycle
notation.  Every function also accepts a list of images, the form the
‘combinatorics’ package uses: ‘[2,1,3]’ sends 1 to 2, 2 to 1 and 3 to 3.
A ‘pgrp_perm’ keeps its degree, and equal permutations of the same
degree are the same value, so ‘=’, ‘member’, ‘unique’ and ‘setify’ work
on them.

