 -- Function: pgrp_compose (S, T, ...)
     Composes permutations right to left: ‘pgrp_compose(s, t)’ applies
     ‘t’ first, then ‘s’.

     This is s∘t in Dummit and Foote's notation.  With more arguments,
     ‘pgrp_compose(a, b, c)’ is a∘b∘c, so ‘c’ applies first.
     Permutations of different degrees are padded with fixed points.
     The examples are D&F's products (1 2 3)∘(1 2)(3 4) = (1 3 4) and (1
     2)∘(1 3) = (1 3 2).

