 -- Function: pgrp_cycles (P)
     Returns the disjoint cycles of ‘p’ as lists, leaving out fixed
     points.

     Each cycle starts at its least point, and the cycles come in order
     of their least points.  The identity gives ‘[]’.  The example is
     D&F's permutation of 1, ..., 13 from §1.3.

