 -- Function: pgrp_conjugate (X, G)
     Returns the conjugate g x g^-1.

     Conjugating relabels the points: if ‘x’ has the cycle (a b c), then
     g x g^-1 has the cycle (g(a) g(b) g(c)).  In the example g = (1
     3)(2 4 5) relabels (1 2 3) as (3 4 1), which is (1 3 4).

