1.8 Homomorphisms and isomorphisms
==================================

A homomorphism between permutation groups is fixed by the images of the
generators.  ‘pgrp_hom’ checks that the images define one.

* Menu:

* Function pgrp_hom G H images::
* Function pgrp_hom_apply phi p::
* Function pgrp_hom_p x::
* Function pgrp_kernel phi::
* Function pgrp_image phi::
* Function pgrp_preimage phi K::
* Function pgrp_isomorphism G H::
* Function pgrp_isomorphic_p G H::
* Function pgrp_order_profile G::
* Function pgrp_sign_hom G::


File: permutations.info,  Node: Function pgrp_hom G H images,  Next: Function pgrp_hom_apply phi p,  Up: Homomorphisms and isomorphisms

 -- Function: pgrp_hom (G, H, IMAGES)
     Returns the homomorphism from ‘G’ to ‘H’ that sends the generators
     of ‘G’ to ‘images’.

     ‘images’ lists one element of ‘H’ for each element of
     ‘pgrp_generators(G)’, in that order.  Fails if no homomorphism does
     that.  A homomorphism displays as ‘pgrp_hom(degree m to degree n)’.
     The example squares in Z_4.

* Menu:

     * Examples: Examples 47.


File: permutations.info,  Node: Examples 47,  Up: Homomorphisms and isomorphisms

1.8.1 Examples
--------------

(%i1) Z4 : pgrp_cyclic(4)$
(%i2) sq : pgrp_hom(Z4, Z4, [pgrp_power(first(pgrp_generators(Z4)), 2)]);
(%o2) pgrp_hom(degree 4 to degree 4)
(%i3) pgrp_elements(pgrp_kernel(sq));
