File: permutations.info,  Node: Function pgrp_stabiliser_chain G,  Prev: Function pgrp_abelian_groups n,  Up: Series Sylow subgroups and products

 -- Function: pgrp_stabiliser_chain (G)
     Returns the Schreier-Sims stabiliser chain of ‘G’ as ‘[k, orbit]’
     pairs.

     Each pair is a point k and its orbit under the subgroup that fixes
     every point above k.  The orbit sizes multiply to the order of ‘G’.
     It doesn't list elements, so it works on large groups.

* Menu:

     * Examples: Examples 86.


File: permutations.info,  Node: Examples 86,  Prev: Examples 85,  Up: Examples 74

1.11.1.12 Examples
..................

(%i1) chain : pgrp_stabiliser_chain(pgrp_symmetric(4));
(%o1) [[4, [1, 2, 3, 4]], [3, [1, 2, 3]], [2, [1, 2]]]
(%i2) apply("*", map(lambda([lev], length(lev[2])), chain));
(%o2) 24

See also: ‘pgrp_order’, ‘pgrp_stabiliser’


